Document this build's page persistence (conformance/docs/rust-build.md > `pages-survive`): an open page lives until
it is closed, so a restart or a reopened window brings it back in its slot under a new `id`, and a page handed to the
Mac presenting a session is parked (`parked: true` in `htmlOverlays` and `remoteOverlays`) when that presenter goes,
its answer pending, until the next presenter attaches. Applied after 0020-agent-mail.patch.

